   "treatment_protocol_ch1": "Eight-week-old control or LSD1-mKO mice were single-housed in cages with free access to a vertical running wheel (Shinano Seisakusho) for 38 days. After three days of familiarization, LSD1-KO was induced by tamoxifen injection at a dose of 75 mg/kg for five consecutive days, and running distance was measured during the next 30 days.",
   "growth_protocol_ch1": "Mice were maintained in a temperature-controlled animal facility with a 12-h light/12-h dark cycle and fed ad libitum on a regular diet. All procedures were conducted in accordance with the guidelines of the Animal Care and Use Committee of Kumamoto University.",
   "molecule_ch1": "total RNA",
   "extract_protocol_ch1": "Total RNA from the muscles were extracted using a Trizol reagent (Invitrogen). mRNA was purified using NEBNext Poly(A) mRNA Magnetic Isolation Module (NEB).,cDNA library for sequencing was synthesized using NEB Next Ultra DNA Library Prep Kit for Illumina (NEB) and was sequenced on NextSeq 500 sequencer (Illumina) with 75-bps single-end reads.",
   "data_processing": "Resulting reads were aligned to the UCSC mm10 reference genome by using STAR.,DESeq2 was used for quantification of gene expression changes. Top 1000 genes showing differential expression between the WT and KO mice were extracted from the genes with mean TPM >1 by using median absolute deviation (MAD).,Assembly: mm10,Supplementary files format and content: All_gene_FC.txt in text file format.",
